Z||000000||fogglethorpe||07-29-2001||02:45 PM||||Fond greetings, citizens! If you are reading this,you are wasting valuable time that could otherwise be spent flossing, or spackling that bathroom wall you've been putting off.<BR>My beloved Pop is a frequent contributor to this message board, and speaks highly of it, and the posters on it. (I don't mean paper posters of burned out, gin-soaked English glam rockers that once hanged in my bedroom when I was a mush-headed adolescent). But, I digress...<BR>I do not own a Fiero, but I do own a Nissan, and I figure they're similar enough to qualify my incohesive ramblings here. After all, both cars have wheels, batteries, seats, etc. My Nissan has an airbag (2 whenever I am in it). I assume Fieros were manufactured before the advent of airbags, but that is not to suggest that they are in any way archaic relics. In fact, I consider them quite interesting and sleek machines that seemed to be ahead of their time at the time.(Does that make sense?)<BR>It's not my desire to take up too much thread space, my being new and all...Perhaps in future postings, I will be more coherent and concise. And don't worry, I'm not one of those irritating nitwits that rambles on incessantly about nothing in particular, or posts those stupid pseudo-Gallagherisms like, "Why does the Department of the Interior deal with stuff that's outside?". And, best of all, I'm not a fringe person, who's sole purpose in life is to bring interplanetary funkitude to all those waiting for the mothership.<BR>I guess what I'm really getting at is...ummm, hold on a second...I forgot.<BR>Oh well, hello anyway.<P><P>------------------<BR>I don't think so;therefore, I'm probably not.||||reg||1
